# Design Rules

Before implementing any screen:

1. Read the matching image in docs/.
2. Explain how the implementation maps to the image.
3. Build reusable components.
4. Compare the rendered result against the reference image.
5. Iterate until visually similar.

Never redesign the interface unless explicitly instructed.

# Rules of Engagement

- Before modifying existing files, explain what will change.
- Implement only the requested feature.
- Never modify unrelated files.
- Never leave TODO placeholders.
- Prefer interfaces over concrete implementations.
- Stop and ask before introducing new dependencies.

# Definition of Done

A task is complete only when:

1. TypeScript passes with zero errors.
2. ESLint passes with zero errors or warnings.
3. No runtime console errors.
4. Interactive controls include accessibility labels.
5. Theme tokens are used instead of inline colors.
6. No duplicated UI primitives.
